  "Question": "Let \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\) be the following sums of arithmetic sequences: \\[\\begin{aligned} X &= 10+12+14+\\cdots+100,\\\\ Y &= 12+14+16+\\cdots+102. \\end{aligned}\\] What is the value of \\(Y - X?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(92\\)",
    "B": "\\(98\\)",
    "C": "\\(100\\)",
    "D": "\\(102\\)",
    "E": "\\(112\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Both sums contain every even number from \\(12\\) through \\(100\\). Grouping those shared terms avoids computing either long sum. Let\n\\[\nS=12+14+\\cdots+100.\n\\]\nThen \\(X=10+S\\) and \\(Y=S+102\\), so\n\\[\nY-X=(S+102)-(10+S)=102-10=92.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(92\\), choice A.",
